<!--
  Sleeves Up brand mark: the binary calendar. Nine cells, seven filled, two empty. A day is
  a cell or it is nothing, which is the product's whole thesis as a shape — what you read is
  density, never depth. Nothing here is shaded or ramped; there is no fraction in this file.

  This single file is the launcher foreground, the themed (monochrome) layer and the splash
  icon (windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon in themes.xml). Keep it that way: a second copy of
  the mark is a copy that can drift out of sync, which is exactly how a raster launcher icon
  and a vector splash once shipped as two different logos under one name.

  Geometry is authored in play-store-assets/generate_icons.py, which emits this pathData and
  the matching 512px Play icon from the same numbers. Edit there, not here. Corners are cubic
  Beziers rather than SVG arc commands so PathParser has no flags to interpret.

  A fill, not a stroke: there is no cap, join or mitre to keep in step with the raster, which
  is why the generator needs none of the polygon stroking its predecessor did.

  Sized by the grid's side rather than by its corner distance. A square reaches further at
  the corner than a circle does at its edge for the same apparent size, so matching the old
  ring's presence means a side of 45, not 49; the corner then lands at 29.34 of 33, inside
  the safe circle without the mark reading undersized beside other launcher icons.
-->
